            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The discoid meniscus is a developmental varient which can produce symptoms resembling those of a meniscus lesion. Two cases are described and the literature is reviewed. The clinical features, diagnosis, pathogenesis and treatment of discoid meniscus is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
